GREAT IF YOU LIKE: Co-op, Genuinely great RPG mechanics; An engaging story in an engaging world;
AVOID IF YOU DISLIKE: Dated graphics; Occasionally buggy multiplayer;
This game remains a great example of an RPG that has aged well. The environments are spooky and claustrophobic, the enemy design is decently varied and interesting, the level design is particularly good, and building up your character through item mechanics and skill trees is both intuitive and very rewarding.
The game is technically solid, with hitreg and physics feeling solid. I never felt unfairly treated by any game mechanic. Coming in at around ten hours, it's a good length of co-op experience, and is best played on the hardest difficulty with one friend, each of you taking a different character class.

